      "side": 1,
      "message": "Issue 1 of b/541328749 still affects driver mode when already in G3:\nIn `zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx/common_pwrseq_host_command.c`, `host_command_reboot_ap_on_g3()` calls `request_start_from_g3()` (line 15) *before* `set_start_from_g3_delay_seconds(cmd-\u003ereboot_ap_at_g3_delay)` (line 22). If the AP is already in `AP_POWER_STATE_G3` when the host command runs, line 77 (`if (start_from_g3_delay_ms)`) sees `0`, immediately posts `AP_PWRSEQ_EVENT_POWER_STARTUP`, and leaves `start_from_g3_delay_ms` stale for the *next* G3 entry.\n\nRecommended fix in `zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx/common_pwrseq_host_command.c`:\n```c\nstatic enum ec_host_cmd_status\nhost_command_reboot_ap_on_g3(struct ec_host_cmd_handler_args *args)\n{\n\tconst struct ec_params_reboot_ap_on_g3_v1 *cmd \u003d args-\u003einput_buf;\n\n\tswitch (args-\u003eversion) {\n\tcase 0:\n\t\tbreak;\n\tcase 1:\n\t\t/* Store user specified delay to wait in G3 state */\n\t\tset_start_from_g3_delay_seconds(cmd-\u003ereboot_ap_at_g3_delay);\n\t\tbreak;\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn EC_HOST_CMD_INVALID_VERSION;\n\t}\n\n\t/* Store request for processing at g3 */\n\trequest_start_from_g3();\n\n\treturn EC_HOST_CMD_SUCCESS;\n}\n```",
